  {
   "id": "UAEuZam-DgAJ",
   "from": "Belay Birlie",
   "author": "e76bf5e76da333a2",
   "date": "2019-10-24T10:40:09Z",
   "subject": "1-1-1 mediation model multilevel approach",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m working on longitudinal mediation analysis where the outcome, treatment of interest, and mediators were repeatedly measured. I have come across this paper <a href=\"http://quantpsy.org/pubs/bauer_preacher_gil_2006.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://quantpsy.org/pubs/bauer_preacher_gil_2006.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859251000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1fyXmExonJq_OI6xP-MGPN\">http://quantpsy.org/pubs/bauer_preacher_gil_2006.pdf</a> which describes the method I want to adopt for my analysis. The have also kindly provided the sas code to the analysis here <a href=\"http://dx.doi.org/10.1037/1082-989X.11.2.142.supp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dx.doi.org/10.1037/1082-989X.11.2.142.supp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859251000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1_MsBUI0rSqRraBZrMcFte\">http://dx.doi.org/10.1037/1082-989X.11.2.142.supp</a> . I would like to do the analysis in lavaan (R) rather than sas. Will you be able to direct me to an example resource if any to do this. </div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Belay </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "96P88xlTAAAJ",
   "from": "Joseph Bonito",
   "author": "a225fe7bebd5f312",
   "date": "2019-10-24T19:51:18Z",
   "subject": "Re: 1-1-1 mediation model multilevel approach",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\">Have a look at the mediation page on the Mplus website: <a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/Mediation.shtml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/Mediation.shtml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859252000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Gh_9yF-MMYUEEU_iPQ0G9\">https://www.statmodel.com/Mediation.shtml</a>.  There you’ll find links to Preacher’s Mplus code for models described in Preacher et al. (2010), including 1-1-1. Also have a look at the “Figure it Out” site by Chris Stride linked to that page—it’s a fantastic resource for migrating from Process.  Adapting Mplus code to lavaan is pretty straightforward. I haven’t tried it but the mplus2lavaan function (<a href=\"https://rdrr.io/cran/lavaan/man/mplus2lavaan.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/cran/lavaan/man/mplus2lavaan.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859252000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Ip-gTdrWTUWjBZ3ChwsSH\">https://rdrr.io/cran/lavaan/man/mplus2lavaan.html</a>) might also be helpful.</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\">I should also mention Moon’s ProcessR package and shiny page at <a href=\"https://rpubs.com/cardiomoon/468602\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rpubs.com/cardiomoon/468602&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859252000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2FzoiOwXHqVDfjHCow8SaK\">https://rpubs.com/cardiomoon/468602</a>.  It’s meant to be the R version of Process and estimates most Process models with lavaan.  You can adapt the code as needed.</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\">Here&#39;s an example to get you started:</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><span>I adapted Preacher’s MSEM 1-1-1 Mplus code to lavaan.  See: </span><a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/download/Preacher.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/download/Preacher.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859252000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1x_aMBQEPxv9H9ELjhL6wd\">https://www.statmodel.com/download/Preacher.pdf</a><span>.</span><div><br></div><div>I used Mplus data example 9.5 and renamed the variables so that they correspond to Preacher. The data weren’t meant to illustrate multilevel mediation but it works well enough to see how to model it. </div><div><div><br></div><div><div>mp &lt;- read.table(&quot;<a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/usersguide/chap9/ex9.5.dat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/usersguide/chap9/ex9.5.dat&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859252000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0c2EG7kub0Osq-TCE1yVv9\">https://www.statmodel.com/usersguide/chap9/ex9.5.dat</a>&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>head(mp)</div><div><br></div><div>names(mp) &lt;- c(&quot;y&quot;,&quot;y2&quot;,&quot;x&quot;,&quot;m&quot;,&quot;w&quot;,&quot;clus&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>library(lavaan)</div><div><br></div><div>model &lt;- &#39;</div><div><br></div><div>level: 1</div><div>y ~ x + bw*m</div><div>m ~ aw*x</div><div><br></div><div>level: 2</div><div>y ~ x + bb*m</div><div>m ~ ab*x</div><div><br></div><div>indw := aw*bw</div><div>indb := ab*bb</div><div>&#39;</div><div><br></div><div>model.out &lt;- sem(model, data = mp, cluster = &quot;clus&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>summary(model.out)</div></div></div></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><br></div><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
