     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Thursday, October 24, 2019 at 8:51:18 PM UTC+1, Joseph Bonito wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\">Have a look at the mediation page on the Mplus website: <a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/Mediation.shtml\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/Mediation.shtml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ydupUTDuGbEFP2lrjApMR\">https://www.statmodel.com/Mediation.shtml</a>.  There you’ll find links to Preacher’s Mplus code for models described in Preacher et al. (2010), including 1-1-1. Also have a look at the “Figure it Out” site by Chris Stride linked to that page—it’s a fantastic resource for migrating from Process.  Adapting Mplus code to lavaan is pretty straightforward. I haven’t tried it but the mplus2lavaan function (<a href=\"https://rdrr.io/cran/lavaan/man/mplus2lavaan.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/cran/lavaan/man/mplus2lavaan.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1UGnaQv-5bA56c2Ioifdpg\">https://rdrr.io/cran/lavaan/man/mplus2lavaan.html</a>) might also be helpful.</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\">I should also mention Moon’s ProcessR package and shiny page at <a href=\"https://rpubs.com/cardiomoon/468602\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rpubs.com/cardiomoon/468602&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hwy377Thd2AY1hUtAPYxP\">https://rpubs.com/cardiomoon/468602</a>.  It’s meant to be the R version of Process and estimates most Process models with lavaan.  You can adapt the code as needed.</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\">Here&#39;s an example to get you started:</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><span>I adapted Preacher’s MSEM 1-1-1 Mplus code to lavaan.  See: </span><a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/download/Preacher.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/download/Preacher.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0bet0lcR_vIOMwXfUTELIX\">https://www.statmodel.com/download/Preacher.pdf</a><span>.</span><div><br></div><div>I used Mplus data example 9.5 and renamed the variables so that they correspond to Preacher. The data weren’t meant to illustrate multilevel mediation but it works well enough to see how to model it. </div><div><div><br></div><div><div>mp &lt;- read.table(&quot;<a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/usersguide/chap9/ex9.5.dat\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/usersguide/chap9/ex9.5.dat&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1TrzzPZx7CsKB0FWmSeSuu\">https://www.statmodel.com/usersguide/chap9/ex9.5.dat</a>&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>head(mp)</div><div><br></div><div>names(mp) &lt;- c(&quot;y&quot;,&quot;y2&quot;,&quot;x&quot;,&quot;m&quot;,&quot;w&quot;,&quot;clus&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>library(lavaan)</div><div><br></div><div>model &lt;- &#39;</div><div><br></div><div>level: 1</div><div>y ~ x + bw*m</div><div>m ~ aw*x</div><div><br></div><div>level: 2</div><div>y ~ x + bb*m</div><div>m ~ ab*x</div><div><br></div><div>indw := aw*bw</div><div>indb := ab*bb</div><div>&#39;</div><div><br></div><div>model.out &lt;- sem(model, data = mp, cluster = &quot;clus&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>summary(model.out)</div></div></div></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px\"><br></div><br></div></blockquote></div>"
