     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m working on longitudinal mediation analysis where the outcome, treatment of interest, and mediators were repeatedly measured. I have come across this paper <a href=\"http://quantpsy.org/pubs/bauer_preacher_gil_2006.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://quantpsy.org/pubs/bauer_preacher_gil_2006.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859255000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ktz0uIA0fC7LiH3NpJoNT\">http://quantpsy.org/pubs/bauer_preacher_gil_2006.pdf</a> which describes the method I want to adopt for my analysis. The have also kindly provided the sas code to the analysis here <a href=\"http://dx.doi.org/10.1037/1082-989X.11.2.142.supp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dx.doi.org/10.1037/1082-989X.11.2.142.supp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859255000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0cm3c6cBptsph3KiM6ZOH5\">http://dx.doi.org/10.1037/1082-989X.11.2.142.supp</a> . I would like to do the analysis in lavaan (R) rather than sas. Will you be able to direct me to an example resource if any to do this. </div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Belay </div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
