    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#080\"><br><br><br>level: 1<br>y ~ x + bw*m<br>m ~ aw*x<br><br><br>level: 2<br></span></div></code></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#080\">y ~ sc*x + bb*m<br>m ~ ab*x<br><br><br>#estimate the mean of aw and call it a<br>aw~a*1<br>#estimate the mean of bw and call it b<br>bw~b*1<br><br><br># estimate Level-2 covariances of aw with sc, m, and y <br>aw~~sc+m+y<br># estimate Level-2 covariances of bw with aw, m, and y <br>bw~~sc+m+y<br>#estimate Level-2 covariances of sc with m and y <br>sc~~m+y<br>#estimate Level-2 covariance of y and m<br>y~~m<br><br><br>#estimate Level-2 covariance of aw and bw, call it &quot;cab&quot;<br>aw~~cab*bw<br><br><br>ind:=aw*bw+cab</span></div></code></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#080\"><br>indw := aw*bw<br>indb := ab*bb<br>&#39;</span></div></code></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cluster </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;clus&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div></div></code></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><br></blockquote></blockquote><div><br></div><br>On Friday, October 25, 2019 at 9:51:47 AM UTC+1, Joseph Bonito wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">As a followup to my previous post, I adapted Preacher’s MSEM 1-1-1 Mplus code to lavaan.  See: <a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/download/Preacher.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/download/Preacher.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859258000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1SrV9xAQqPk0hk8BuRtvbU\">https://www.statmodel.com/download/Preacher.pdf</a>.</div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><br></div><div>I used Mplus data example 9.5 and renamed the variables so that they correspond to Preacher. The data weren’t meant to illustrate multilevel mediation but it works well enough to see how to model it. </div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><br><div><br></div><div><div>mp &lt;- read.table(&quot;<a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/usersguide/chap9/ex9.5.dat\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/usersguide/chap9/ex9.5.dat&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859258000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gMe36CNpPLueq9zz91BmP\">https://www.statmodel.com/usersguide/chap9/ex9.5.dat</a>&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>head(mp)</div><div><br></div><div>names(mp) &lt;- c(&quot;y&quot;,&quot;y2&quot;,&quot;x&quot;,&quot;m&quot;,&quot;w&quot;,&quot;clus&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>library(lavaan)</div><div><br></div><div>model &lt;- &#39;</div><div><br></div><div>level: 1</div><div>y ~ x + bw*m</div><div>m ~ aw*x</div><div><br></div><div>level: 2</div><div>y ~ x + bb*m</div><div>m ~ ab*x</div><div><br></div><div>indw := aw*bw</div><div>indb := ab*bb</div><div>&#39;</div><div><br></div><div>model.out &lt;- sem(model, data = mp, cluster = &quot;clus&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>summary(model.out)</div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Oct 24, 2019, at 3:40 AM, Belay Birlie &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">belaya...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m working on longitudinal mediation analysis where the outcome, treatment of interest, and mediators were repeatedly measured. I have come across this paper <a href=\"http://quantpsy.org/pubs/bauer_preacher_gil_2006.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://quantpsy.org/pubs/bauer_preacher_gil_2006.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859258000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3vH0jcCXxvob63xlVCswXK\">http://quantpsy.org/pubs/bauer_preacher_gil_2006.pdf</a> which describes the method I want to adopt for my analysis. The have also kindly provided the sas code to the analysis here <a href=\"http://dx.doi.org/10.1037/1082-989X.11.2.142.supp\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dx.doi.org/10.1037/1082-989X.11.2.142.supp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422859258000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1eCtp74WpLugtqiHZy-kJk\">http://dx.doi.org/10.1037/1082-989X.11.2.142.supp</a> . I would like to do the analysis in lavaan (R) rather than sas. Will you be able to direct me to an example resource if any to do this. </div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Belay </div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
